# Files kept in the repo but never uploaded to the deployment.
#
# tools/ is internal enforcement tooling. The measurement method is not
# published. Restoring measure-specimen.py so the README's rule stayed
# enforceable also put it back on a public URL — /tools/measure-specimen.py
# and /tools/baseline.json both answered 200 — because this repo is served
# as-is. The repo keeps the scripts; the deployment does not get them.
tools/

# Same reasoning as tools/. The verification harness and the recorded baseline
# are internal: this repo is uploaded as-is, so anything left here answers 200
# on the public site. scripts/ would publish the checks, baseline/ and
# verification/ would publish the screenshots and the Lighthouse traces, and
# package.json would advertise a build step the deployment does not have.
scripts/
baseline/
verification/
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/
